WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.900
In 1990, around 2.3 billion
people lived below the World

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.430
Bank's line for extreme poverty.

3
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:12.640
By 2025, the estimate
was around 831 million.

4
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.140
That is about 1 in 10
people on the planet.

5
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.960
So when people get richer,

6
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.260
poverty falls. Simple.

7
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.510
Or is it?

8
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.150
Picture a country where almost
every family's income goes up,

9
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.790
year after year.

10
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.520
Could more people end up counted as poor?

11
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.640
In this mission, you'll line up
households from lowest income to highest,

12
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.510
and draw a poverty line.

13
00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.040
Then you'll see why one
country can report two

14
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.970
different poverty figures
for the same year.

15
00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.090
Your mission: find out what it
really means to be counted as poor.
